- **Operational Bridge:** Name the observable dynamic tentatively, invite correction, propose a constructive frame, and hold steady vocal pacing so the new frame sticks.
- **Office Worked Example:** *“We've spent twenty minutes trading reasons why Friday won't work—I wonder if we're actually stuck on unclear priority order rather than effort. What if we rank the top two deliverables together for five minutes?”*
- **Personal Worked Example:** *“I notice we're going back and forth on logistics when both of us sound drained from the week—do we want to keep planning tonight, or just pick something easy and catch up?”*
- **Non-Example:** Delivering a sweeping psychological verdict on the group (*“You're all avoiding accountability because of ego”*) without tentativeness or an invitation to correct.
- **Decision Rule & Handoff:** Keep every pattern-naming **observable, tentative, and blame-free**, and always pair a reframe with one concrete next step. Feeds Friday's **Systemic Steering Map**.

